frequency: 130
is-card: true
tags: international

= Our Man in Moscow

The Zentrale's representative at the Executive lives in the Hotel Lux and writes every week. The Executive is five men, he reminds us, and each reads the German reports for something different. He asks whose door he should knock on this month. [? if ecci_friend_name : Our best friend there is [+ ecci_friend_name +]. ?]

- @lenin: Take Lenin the facts he always asks for.
- @zinoviev: Pledge discipline to Zinoviev.
- @radek: Tell Radek the Berlin gossip.
- @trotsky: Give Trotsky a report on the Reichswehr.
- @easy_discard

@lenin
subtitle: Sixty pages on wages, prices and the unions. Lenin is pleased, and Zinoviev notices who was asked.
view-if: ecci_lenin_ill = 0
on-arrival: {!
RG.ecci('lenin', 10);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -3);
!}

The report comes back with pencil marks in the margins, and one note at the end: "Good. More of this."

@zinoviev
subtitle: The President likes obedience, and our independence pays for it.
on-arrival: {!
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 10);
Q.independence -= 5;
!}

The letter promises iron discipline and the struggle against every deviation. It is a letter Zinoviev likes to read aloud.

@radek
subtitle: Radek likes to know everything first. Some of it may come back to Berlin, with names.
on-arrival: {!
RG.ecci('radek', 10);
if (Math.random() < 0.3) { Q.lw_out = 1; Q.unity -= 4; }
!}

[? if lw_out = 1 : A month later, half of it is repeated at a session of the Executive, and the German comrades concerned are not amused. ?][? if lw_out = 0 : Radek laughs a great deal, and promises to put in a word. ?]

@trotsky
subtitle: The Commissar for War values hard information. The police would value it too.
on-arrival: {!
RG.ecci('trotsky', 10);
Q.repression += 2;
!}

The report lists the Reichswehr's garrisons, its secret reserves and the officers who drink too much. Trotsky sends back a short letter of thanks and a longer list of questions.
